   "subject": "Re: Can you fix this error with MKL library in 3.2.3",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi George,</div><div><br></div><div>Good job on resolving the issue yourself, I would like to share here the correct procedure to install/uninstall MRO and MKL for future reference.</div><div><br></div><div>Uninstallation:</div><ol><li><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">First, uninstall MKL Math Libraries. This will revert to the original </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Rblas.dll</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> and </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Rlapack.dll</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> files.</font></li><li><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Remove the </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">RevoMath</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> package using the Windows instructions for uninstalling a program specific to your version of Windows. For example, on Windows 8.1, choose </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Control Panel &gt; Programs &amp; Features &gt; Uninstall</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">.</font></li><li><p><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Find </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">RevoMath</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> in the list and uninstall.</font></p></li><li><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Then, uninstall Microsoft R Open :</font></li><li><p><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Remove Microsoft R Open using the Windows instructions for uninstalling a program specific to your version of Windows. For example, on Windows 8, choose </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Control Panel &gt; Programs &amp; Features &gt; Uninstall</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">.</font></p></li><li><p><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Find </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">MRO for Windows 3.2.3</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> in the list and uninstall.</font></p></li><li><p><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Remove the directory in which you installed Microsoft R Open, by default </font><code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">C:\\Program Files\\MicrosoftMRO</font></code><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\">.</font></p></li></ol><p><font size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"2\">Installation:</font></p><ol><li><font size=\"2\">Launch the Microsoft R Open installer and follow the prompts.</font></li><li><font size=\"2\">After installing Microsoft R Open, you can enable the optional multi-threaded performance for Microsoft R Open as follows:<div><strong>Warning! </strong> Install Microsoft R Open first before MKL. If you reinstall Microsoft R Open without removing MKL, your MKL will no longer work. Instead, you must first uninstall MKL first as described above  </div><p>A. <a href=\"https://mran.microsoft.com/download/#download\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://mran.microsoft.com/download/%23download&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241532346000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0s5rrwat9Y8g3SBrD7OcHx\"><u><font color=\"#0066cc\">Download</font></u></a> the Math Kernel Library (MKL) corresponding for this release of Microsoft R Open.</p><p>B. Go to the directory into which you downloaded <code>RevoMath-3.2.3.exe</code>, the MKL utility.</p><p>C. Launch the installer and follow the prompts. </p></font></li></ol><p><font size=\"2\">Thanks,</font></p><p><font size=\"2\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"2\">Smit</font></p></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br> <br>On Friday, April 8, 2016 at 2:57:08 PM UTC-5, George Carlisle wrote:</div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I love self-service...</div><div><br></div><div>You must uninstall the older versions of Microsoft Open R. I had 3.2.2 and reboot your machine. I have successfully solved my own problems...</div><div><br></div><div>1. Install 3.2.3</div><div>2. Install MKL</div><div>3. Success startup with both functioning</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-right:1em;margin-left:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-odNwwfa02Rc/VwgMtg5FE9I/AAAAAAAABHc/oxwj-p27EBkOj-gT2Ut2hel-iHifIa04w/s1600/microsoft-R3.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-odNwwfa02Rc/VwgMtg5FE9I/AAAAAAAABHc/oxwj-p27EBkOj-gT2Ut2hel-iHifIa04w/s1600/microsoft-R3.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241532347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2j0gmnGm0th5Ifejbui-BU\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-odNwwfa02Rc/VwgMtg5FE9I/AAAAAAAABHc/oxwj-p27EBkOj-gT2Ut2hel-iHifIa04w/s1600/microsoft-R3.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-right:1em;margin-left:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-mlplFMQKsn0/VwgM-DJsX6I/AAAAAAAABHg/A1AMFdKt7BEwaWBRwJBhvUXzP2uH2fmzg/s1600/microsoft-R4.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-mlplFMQKsn0/VwgM-DJsX6I/AAAAAAAABHg/A1AMFdKt7BEwaWBRwJBhvUXzP2uH2fmzg/s1600/microsoft-R4.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241532347000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Y4ZURowaMPpQxNl67q9cr\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-mlplFMQKsn0/VwgM-DJsX6I/AAAAAAAABHg/A1AMFdKt7BEwaWBRwJBhvUXzP2uH2fmzg/s1600/microsoft-R4.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p